From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:53:35 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Add wlr-output-management tests

Two test monitors, the first with 1920x1080@60 in a fixed and a
variable refresh rate variant, 1280x720 and 1024x768, the second with
1024x768. A test client lists the heads, then tests and applies
configurations while the compositor side checks the monitor manager's
state after each step:

- the listing folds the two 1920x1080 variants into one mode;
- test changes nothing, apply changes both monitors at once;
- adaptive sync picks the variable refresh rate mode, and is refused for
  a mode without one;
- one bad head, or a gap between the heads, fails the configuration and
  changes nothing;
- transform and position, mirroring (one logical monitor), disabling and
  re-enabling with defaults (preferred mode, placed to the right);
- a configuration made before a hotplug is cancelled, and the unplugged
  head and its modes are finished.

Two more cases check that the already_set and unconfigured_head protocol
errors leave the monitors alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
